meta {
  name: replace blog
  type: http
  seq: 31
}

put {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/blogs/:id/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 5c1e8a2f-9d43-4b76-8e0a-1f2c3d4e5a6b
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required.
    "title_en": "Five Spanish Phrases That Instantly Make You Sound Local in Quito",

    // Optional, but omitting any of these clears it.
    "title_es": "",
    "slug": "five-spanish-phrases-that-instantly-make-you-sound-local-in-quito",
    "excerpt_en": "Textbook Spanish will get you understood. These five phrases will get you smiled at.",
    "excerpt_es": "",
    "body_en": "<p>Textbook Spanish will get you understood...</p>",
    "body_es": "",
    "image_urls": [],
    "category": "spanish_learning_tips",
    "status": "published",
    "meta_title": "",
    "meta_description": ""
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  `PUT` **replaces** the record: any writable field you leave out is reset to its
  default or blank, not left alone. Use `PATCH` (see **update blog**) unless you are
  deliberately sending the whole object -- an edit form that omits a field will
  silently wipe it.

  Particularly worth care here: omitting `body_en` blanks the article.

  `slug`, `reading_time` and the author stay server-managed either way, and
  `published_at` is still stamped only on the first publish.

  ## API example response
  {
    "id": "5c1e8a2f-9d43-4b76-8e0a-1f2c3d4e5a6b",
    "title_en": "Five Spanish Phrases That Instantly Make You Sound Local in Quito",
    "slug": "five-spanish-phrases-that-instantly-make-you-sound-local-in-quito",
    "status": "published",
    "published_at": "2026-09-05T08:44:12.512000-05:00",
    "reading_time": 4,
    "lang": "en",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-12T10:20:00.000000-05:00"
  }
}
